WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.950
Six Moves, from EL Publishing. Move four: word bank, frame, model.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.191
You give a writing prompt: explain how a plant cell is different from an animal cell.

3
00:00:10.191 --> 00:00:14.926
Your English learners write nothing. Or two sentences. The prompt isn't the problem.

4
00:00:14.926 --> 00:00:16.448
The blank page under it is.

5
00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:22.423
No vocabulary, no structure, no example — it's the writing equivalent of saying, go talk for five minutes.

6
00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:26.507
The move is three things on the page before anyone writes a word.

7
00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:31.842
One: a word bank. The eight or ten words they'll need, right there on the page.

8
00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:35.675
Cell wall, chloroplast, membrane, nucleus, both, only, unlike.

9
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:40.796
Two: a frame, or a structure. Both cells have blank. Only a plant cell has blank.

10
00:00:40.796 --> 00:00:43.218
Unlike an animal cell, a plant cell blank.

11
00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:46.909
That's a compare paragraph with the grammar already standing up.

12
00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:48.143
Three: a model.

13
00:00:48.143 --> 00:00:55.146
One paragraph that you wrote, about a different topic — say, a bike and a car — so they can see the shape without copying the content.

14
00:00:55.596 --> 00:01:01.867
Word bank, frame, model. With those three, a level two writes a paragraph. Without them, nobody does.

15
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:06.326
And know what good looks like at each level, so you can be happy with it.

16
00:01:06.326 --> 00:01:11.269
A level one labels the diagram and copies two frame sentences — that's writing, it counts.

17
00:01:11.269 --> 00:01:14.619
A level two gives you four or five sentences from the frames.

18
00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:18.573
A level three writes the paragraph from the word bank and the structure.

19
00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:24.285
A level four writes from the model alone, and you push on connectors: however, as a result, which means.

20
00:01:24.735 --> 00:01:29.866
Here is a level-two paragraph. Both cells have a nucleus. Both cells have a membrane.

21
00:01:29.866 --> 00:01:34.091
Only a plant cell has a cell wall. Only a plant cell has chloroplasts.

22
00:01:34.091 --> 00:01:37.411
Unlike an animal cell, a plant cell makes its own food.

23
00:01:37.411 --> 00:01:43.025
Five sentences, correct science, correct English, from a student who wrote nothing in August.

24
00:01:43.025 --> 00:01:44.353
That is a win. Say so.

25
00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:50.828
One more thing. When you mark it, pick one thing. This week it's capital letters. Next week it's because.

26
00:01:50.828 --> 00:01:55.132
Fourteen red corrections teach a level two exactly one lesson: don't write.

27
00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.857
Tomorrow: take your next prompt and put the three things on the page.

28
00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:04.627
The EL Assistants on the hub will draft the word bank and the frames for you.

29
00:02:04.627 --> 00:02:07.973
Free, at radan55 dot github dot io slash everyteacher.
